---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { EMAILS } from '../config';

// Table of contents — ids must match the h2 ids below.
const toc = [
  { id: 'what-are-cookies', title: 'What are cookies?' },
  { id: 'how-we-use-cookies', title: 'How we use cookies' },
  { id: 'the-cookies-we-use', title: 'The cookies we use' },
  { id: 'your-consent-choices', title: 'Your consent choices' },
  { id: 'third-party-cookies', title: 'Third-party cookies' },
  { id: 'browser-controls', title: 'Browser controls' },
  { id: 'changes-to-this-policy', title: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact-us', title: 'Contact us' },
];

const privacyEmail = EMAILS.privacy;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="How Handsful uses cookies and similar tracking technologies on handsful.app."
  placeholder={false}
  noindex={true}
  lastUpdated="July 12, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains how MESQUITE &amp; THORN DIGITAL, LLC (doing business as Handsful)
    ("<strong>we</strong>," "<strong>us</strong>," or "<strong>our</strong>") uses cookies and
    similar tracking technologies on
    <a href="https://www.handsful.app">https://www.handsful.app</a> (the
    "<strong>Website</strong>"). It supplements our Privacy Policy at
    <a href="/privacy-policy">https://www.handsful.app/privacy-policy</a>. Terms not defined here
    have the meaning given in the Privacy Policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy currently covers the Website only. The Handsful mobile app does not yet use
    cookies or the tracking technologies described here; if that changes, this policy will be
    updated and you will be notified through the app.
  </p>

  <h2 id="table-of-contents">Table of contents</h2>
  <ol class="toc">
    {
      toc.map(({ id, title }) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <h2 id="what-are-cookies">1. What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. They're widely
    used to make websites work, work more efficiently, and to provide reporting information.
    Similar technologies (like local storage) serve comparable purposes and are covered by this
    policy alongside cookies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-we-use-cookies">2. How we use cookies</h2>
  <p>We use two categories of cookies on the Website:</p>
  <p>
    <strong>Essential cookies</strong> — required for the Website to function. These don't require
    consent and can't be turned off through our banner. They include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your cookie consent choice itself (so we remember your preference and don't ask again every
      visit)
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Analytics cookies</strong> — used only with your consent, to help us understand how
    visitors use the Website (e.g. which pages are viewed, general traffic patterns). We use
    Google Analytics (GA4) for this purpose. See
    <a href="#your-consent-choices">Section 4</a> for how consent controls this.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. We do not sell or share data
    collected through cookies with third parties for advertising purposes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-cookies-we-use">3. The cookies we use</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Cookie/Technology</th>
          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
          <th scope="col">Type</th>
          <th scope="col">Duration</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>handsful_cookie_consent</code> (localStorage, not a cookie)</td>
          <td>Stores your cookie preference so we don't ask again</td>
          <td>Essential</td>
          <td>12 months, after which we ask again</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga</code></td>
          <td>Distinguishes unique visitors (Google Analytics)</td>
          <td>Analytics — requires consent</td>
          <td>2 years</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga_PJC1SRJSPB</code></td>
          <td>Persists session state (Google Analytics 4)</td>
          <td>Analytics — requires consent</td>
          <td>2 years</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    This table will be updated if additional cookies or tracking technologies are added to the
    Website.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-consent-choices">4. Your consent choices</h2>
  <p>
    When you first visit the Website, a consent banner asks whether you'd like to allow analytics
    cookies. Google Analytics is configured to deny data collection by default (via Google Consent
    Mode) — it collects nothing about you unless and until you actively accept.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>If you accept</strong>, analytics cookies are enabled and GA4 begins collecting
      anonymized usage data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>If you decline</strong>, only essential cookies are used, and GA4 collects nothing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To change your choice at any time</strong>, use the "Cookie preferences" link in the
      Website footer, which reopens the consent banner.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your choice is stored so you won't be asked again on future visits unless you clear your
    browser's storage, use a different browser/device, or more than 12 months has passed since
    you last chose — after which we'll ask again to keep your consent current.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party-cookies">5. Third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Google Analytics (GA4) is the only third-party service that sets cookies on the Website, and
    only after you consent. For more on how Google handles data, see
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Google's Privacy Policy</a
    > and information on
    <a
      href="https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/collection/analyticsjs/cookie-usage"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics cookie usage</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 id="browser-controls">6. Browser controls</h2>
  <p>
    Most browsers let you block or delete cookies through their settings, independent of the
    choice you make in our banner. Blocking essential cookies may affect how the Website functions
    (for example, we may not remember your consent preference, and the banner may reappear on
    every visit).
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes-to-this-policy">7. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Cookie Policy as our use of cookies changes, including when the Handsful
    mobile app introduces cookies or similar tracking technologies. The "Last updated" date above
    reflects the most recent revision.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact-us">8. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this Cookie Policy can be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>, or by mail to:
  </p>
  <p>
    MESQUITE &amp; THORN DIGITAL, LLC<br />
    Data Protection Officer<br />
    1018 E Washington St, Suite A<br />
    Brownsville, TX 78520<br />
    United States
  </p>
</LegalLayout>

<!-- Shared legal typography (TOC, lists, tables, scroll margins) lives in
     LegalLayout.astro's :global styles. -->
